data.content:
## EF Core 10 Breaking Changes for Your Code

### 1. `SetProperty` — value parameter must now be a lambda

EF Core 10 removed the overload accepting a raw `TProperty` value. Both arguments must be `Expression<Func<TSource, TProperty>>`:

```csharp
// Before (EF Core 9)
s => s.SetProperty(b => b.Views, 8)

// After (EF Core 10) — value wrapped in lambda
s => s.SetProperty(b => b.Views, b => 8)
```

**Fix for your expression tree building:**

```csharp
var blogParameter = Expression.Parameter(typeof(Blog), "b");
var valueParameter = Expression.Parameter(typeof(Blog), "b");

setters = Expression.Lambda<Func<SetPropertyCalls<Blog>, SetPropertyCalls<Blog>>>(
    Expression.Call(
        instance: setters.Body,
        methodName: nameof(SetPropertyCalls<Blog>.SetProperty),
        typeArguments: new[] { typeof(string) },
        arguments: new Expression[]
        {
            Expression.Lambda<Func<Blog, string>>(
                Expression.Property(blogParameter, nameof(Blog.Name)), blogParameter),
            // Wrap the constant in a lambda: b => "foo"
            Expression.Lambda<Func<Blog, string>>(
                Expression.Constant("foo"), valueParameter)
        }),
    setters.Parameters);
```

---

### 2. Complex types — duplicate property names now require explicit column configuration

EF Core 10 no longer silently disambiguates columns when multiple complex properties share CLR property names. You must configure column names explicitly:

```csharp
modelBuilder.Entity<Customer>(b =>
{
    b.ComplexProperty(c => c.ShippingAddress, ab =>
    {
        ab.Property(a => a.Street).HasColumnName("ShippingStreet");
    });
    b.ComplexProperty(c => c.BillingAddress, ab =>
    {
        ab.Property(a => a.Street).HasColumnName("BillingStreet");
    });
});

// Nested complex types — same principle:
modelBuilder.Entity<Order>(b =>
{
    b.ComplexProperty(o => o.Payment, pb =>
    {
        pb.ComplexProperty(p => p.BillingAddress, ab =>
        {
            ab.Property(a => a.City).HasColumnName("PaymentBillingCity");
        });
    });
});
```

---

### 3. `IRelationalCommandDiagnosticsLogger` — new `CommandSource` parameter

EF Core 10 added a `CommandSource` parameter to the interface methods:

```csharp
public class MyLogger : IRelationalCommandDiagnosticsLogger
{
    public InterceptionResult<DbDataReader> CommandReaderExecuting(
        IRelationalConnection connection,
        DbCommand command,
        DbContext context,
        Guid commandId,
        Guid connectionId,
        DateTimeOffset startTime,
        CommandSource commandSource)   // ← new parameter
    { /* logging */ }
}
```

Add the parameter to every method in the interface you implement (`CommandReaderExecuting`, `CommandScalarExecuting`, `CommandNonQueryExecuting`, and their async counterparts).

---

### Summary

| Area | Change | Action |
|------|--------|--------|
| `SetProperty` | Raw-value overload removed | Wrap values in `b => value` lambdas |
| Complex types | Ambiguous column names throw | Add explicit `HasColumnName()` |
| Diagnostics logger | `CommandSource` param added | Add parameter to all method signatures |
